<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/meeting-table.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/meeting-table-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/meeting-table.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="shell sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/">Services</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Clause Representation</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Appraisal Clause Representation for Utah Policyholders</h1><p class="lede">Your insurer agrees the loss is covered but its number won’t rebuild what was damaged. When either side demands appraisal, you need an appraiser who can defend every line. That is the role we fill.</p><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Our role</dt><dd>Your selected appraiser</dd></div><div><dt>Panel</dt><dd>2 appraisers + umpire</dd></div><div><dt>Decides</dt><dd>Amount of loss only</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="shell two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>A short clause with long consequences</h2>
<p>Most homeowners and commercial property policies sold in Utah include a condition titled “Appraisal.” The wording varies by carrier, but the structure is familiar: if you and the insurer fail to agree on the amount of loss, either side can demand appraisal in writing. Each side picks a competent and impartial appraiser. The two appraisers pick an umpire. A written agreement signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss.</p>
<p>That final step is the reason this clause matters. Appraisal is not mediation and it is not a suggestion. A properly signed award fixes the dollar value of the covered damage, so the quality of the file your appraiser builds before that signature is everything.</p>
<h2>What we handle once we’re appointed</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Policy and demand review.</strong> We read the appraisal condition, the demand letter and any carrier correspondence so we know exactly what is in dispute and what deadlines apply.</li>
<li><strong>Our own inspection.</strong> We measure, photograph and scope the property from scratch. We don’t start from the carrier’s estimate and adjust it; we start from the building.</li>
<li><strong>Line-item valuation.</strong> We price the repair in industry estimating software at current Utah material and labor costs for your area, including the code items, access and trade coordination your property actually needs.</li>
<li><strong>Working the panel.</strong> We meet with the insurer’s appraiser, walk the property together where possible, and narrow the dispute line by line.</li>
<li><strong>Umpire submission.</strong> If items remain open, we help select a qualified umpire and present the remaining differences with photos, measurements and pricing support.</li>
<li><strong>Award review.</strong> Before anything is signed, we make sure replacement cost, actual cash value and depreciation are spelled out so the award can be paid without confusion.</li>
</ol>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Know the limits</b>Appraisal resolves how much a covered loss costs. It doesn’t decide coverage, and it doesn’t award damages for how a claim was handled. If your claim was denied outright, speak with a Utah attorney before, or instead of, hiring an appraiser.</div>
<h2>Utah claims where representation tends to help</h2>
<p>We see appraisal work well on Utah hail claims where the carrier approved a few slopes instead of the whole roof, on canyon-wind losses where siding and fencing were scoped too narrowly, and on winter water losses where drying and rebuild costs were underpriced. It is a weaker fit when the real argument is about an exclusion, such as wear and tear, settling or a late-notice position.</p>
<h2>Why we price conservatively</h2>
<p>An appraiser who inflates a number may look good in the first meeting and then lose the umpire. We build valuations we can defend under questioning, because a credible number is the one that moves an award.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can my roofer be my appraiser?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Most appraisal clauses require an impartial or disinterested appraiser. Someone who will profit from the repair contract can give the other side grounds to challenge the award, so it’s usually safer to choose an independent appraiser.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if the insurer won’t agree to appraisal?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>If the policy has an appraisal clause and the disagreement is truly about the amount of loss, a written demand normally starts the process. Disputes about coverage may fall outside appraisal. If the carrier refuses, a Utah attorney can advise on your options.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does a Utah appraisal usually take?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>A straightforward residential claim often wraps up within two to three months of both appraisers being named. Large commercial losses or files that need an umpire hearing can take longer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Homeowner Claim Appraisal</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-ser